// Code only developers' tools or tests run.
//
// A dev or test build compiles more than the product: Mix tasks and the
// helpers they share, a project's test support, the test helpers a
// library ships in its own lib/, a development-only seed or dashboard.
// A defect there costs a developer's command or a test run, not the
// running system, and every analysis steps its finding down one level
// (Argus.Findings.Tooling, by the finding's module).
//
// tooling(mod, basis, permille): the module is tooling because its
// name or source path says so (`tooling_module`: basis "mix" or
// "test_support", permille 1000), or because the tooling prior is sure
// of it (basis "prior": the probability that it is a developer's tool
// or test support, at 0.9 or more; Argus.Priors.Questions.Tooling). The
// prior is asked only about modules the structure leaves undecided, and
// a module the prior is unsure of stays the product: the word errs
// quiet, toward the structural severity.
//
// An analysis includes this file and declares `.output tooling`; its
// rows re-tier the analysis's findings and are no findings themselves.

.decl tooling(mod: symbol, basis: symbol, permille: number)

tooling(m, basis, 1000) :- tooling_module(m, basis).

// 0.9 is where the calibration measured 8 of 9 re-tiers right over the
// modules holding a finding in the evaluation programs.
tooling(m, "prior", p) :-
  prior_tooling(m, _, _, p),
  p >= 900,
  !tooling_module(m, _).
